        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 191,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Calculate the magnitude of the given cross product vector $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$. We have $\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{3^2 + 2^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 4 + 36} = \\sqrt{49} = 7$."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 820,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 821,
        "char_start": 523,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 297,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 298,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Substitute the known values into the cross product magnitude formula to solve for $\\sin(\\theta)$. We know $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = 2$, $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = 7$, and $\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = 7$. Therefore, $7 = 2 \\cdot 7 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)$, which simplifies to $\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2}$."
      },
